# 34. EXAM TRAPS

> **"Large network traffic = data theft."**

False.

> **"HTTPS prevents exfiltration."**

False.

HTTPS protects traffic contents in transit but does not prevent an authorized or compromised endpoint from sending data.

> **"DNS is only used for domain resolution."**

False.

DNS can be abused for various malicious purposes.

> **"DLP automatically stops every data leak."**

False.

DLP effectiveness depends on configuration, visibility, policies, and the nature of the data.

